WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.373 --> 00:00:02.560
Speaker 1: but also have to&nbsp;
talk about one more thing here.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.920
Biden's done some good. OK, we can't just sit&nbsp;
here and say, Oh, build back better is dead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:13.040
And Biden's not doing anything for young young&nbsp;
voters, whatever it is, because Biden has done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:19.040
one thing that is truly phenomenal, that he is&nbsp;
unfortunately not getting enough credit for.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:24.400
And I do believe in giving credit where credit's&nbsp;
due, and that is appointing federal judges&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:31.520
since the Senate is out for the year now. Biden,&nbsp;
in his first year in office, has gotten confirmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:38.560
40 federal judges to lifetime appointments here in&nbsp;
the United States. That is more than any president&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:44.240
in their first year in office since Ronald&nbsp;
Reagan. And by the way, it's more than double&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:51.760
what Donald Trump got in his first year in office&nbsp;
when he had the Senate under Republican control.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.880
That's pretty remarkable. But it's not&nbsp;
just the number that's remarkable here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.000
because anybody can appoint judges, right,&nbsp;
get the numbers up, you look good. But the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.160
fact? Is that a lot of these&nbsp;
people that Biden has picked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:16.080
are either coming from a background as public&nbsp;
defenders or from plaintiff's law firms?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:23.040
And that's a huge difference from what we even saw&nbsp;
with President Obama. President Obama picked a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:28.880
of people, obviously with the liberal credentials,&nbsp;
but they came from these corporate defense law&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:35.120
firms. And that's why even his administration saw&nbsp;
some of their rules struck down by the very judges&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.840
he put in place for a lifetime because they&nbsp;
benefited consumers rather than corporations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:47.040
These judges, depending on their background, do&nbsp;
obviously have a bias. You cannot say that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:54.400
don't. They're not supposed to, but they&nbsp;
do. And so picking people who spent their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.400 --> 00:02:02.000
careers representing injured people, injured&nbsp;
consumers, and now they get to be the judges.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.960
That is a massive step forward that is huge&nbsp;
for this country. And again, typically this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:14.080
not something that we see even from Democratic&nbsp;
presidents. So Joe Biden, President Joe Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:21.200
deserves a ton of credit for what he is doing with&nbsp;
these federal judges so far in year one, that has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:27.440
absolutely been the brightest spot of this entire&nbsp;
administration. I am Farron Cousins of sitting in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:32.560
for David Pakman. Follow me on Twitter at fair&nbsp;
and Balanced. It will be right back with more.

